If none of the above suggestions of
@ATT_Turan
works for you, you may be able to try this:
JavaScript:
SceneManager.push(Scene_Menu)
window.myInterval = setInterval(function () {
    if(SceneManager._scene.constructor.name === "Scene_Menu" && SceneManager._scene.isReady()){
        SceneManager._scene._commandWindow.selectSymbol("formation")
        SceneManager._scene._commandWindow.callOkHandler()
        clearInterval(window.myInterval)
    }else{

    }
}, 1000);
This will call the Scene Menu and after that make the game keep checking every second if you are on the Scene Menu. When you get there, and the scene is ready, it will automatically select the formation symbol and confirm that selection.
You can change the 1000, to any number you want. That value is in MS, so 1000 MS = 1 Second.

